\begin{abstract}
The Trichological Cycle Engine (TCE) is a sovereign autonomous
biological simulation framework designed to model the full
hair-follicle lifecycle under nominal, stressed, and stochastic
conditions. This white paper formalizes the governing differential
system, phase-transition logic, Lyapunov stability layer, and
supervisory sovereign kernel responsible for real-time recovery
and identity re-indexing.
\end{abstract}

\section{Introduction}
The TCE architecture integrates continuous biological kinetics with
discrete supervisory logic to simulate the Anagen, Catagen, and
Telogen phases of the human hair follicle. The system is designed
for long-duration autonomous operation, incorporating stochastic
perturbations, stress-mode overrides, and sovereign-level recovery
mechanisms.

\section{Governing Dynamics}
Let $F(t)$ denote the follicular vitality index and $\sigma(t)\in\{A,C,T\}$
the active biological phase. The governing differential equation is:
\begin{equation}
\frac{dF}{dt}
= \alpha^\star \mathbb{I}(\sigma=A)
- \beta^\star \mathbb{I}(\sigma=C)
- \gamma \mathbb{I}(\sigma=T)
+ \Delta S(t),
\end{equation}
where $\alpha^\star$, $\beta^\star$ are stress-mode overrides and
$\Delta S(t)$ is a bounded stochastic forcing term.

\section{Phase Transition Logic}
The autonomous phase update is governed by:
\begin{equation}
\sigma(t+\Delta t)=
\begin{cases}
C & \sigma(t)=A,\ F(t)\le\theta_C,\\
T & \sigma(t)=C,\ t_p\ge T_c,\\
A & \sigma(t)=T,\ F(t)\ge\theta_A.
\end{cases}
\end{equation}

\section{Lyapunov Stability Layer}
Define the error coordinate:
\begin{equation}
e(t)=F(t)-F^*,
\end{equation}
and the Lyapunov candidate:
\begin{equation}
V(e)=\frac{1}{2}e^2.
\end{equation}
Nominal dynamics yield:
\begin{equation}
\dot{V}(e)= -\lambda e^2 + e\,\Delta S(t),
\end{equation}
with stability guaranteed whenever:
\begin{equation}
|e| > \frac{\delta_{\max}}{\lambda}.
\end{equation}

\section{Stress Testing Protocol}
Stress-mode overrides are defined as:
\begin{align}
\alpha^\star &= \Pi_{\text{override}}(\alpha),\\
\beta^\star &= \Pi_{\text{override}}(\beta),\\
T_c^\star &= \Pi_{\text{override}}(T_c),
\end{align}
with stochastic forcing modeled as an Ornstein-Uhlenbeck process.

\section{Sovereign Kernel Recovery}
Failure conditions $\mathcal{F}_i$ trigger the sovereign purge operator:
\begin{equation}
(F^+,\sigma^+,\hat{\Lambda}^+)=\mathcal{P}_{\text{sov}}(F,\sigma,\hat{\Lambda}),
\end{equation}
forcing re-entry into the Lyapunov basin around $F^*$.

\section{Conclusion}
The TCE constitutes a fully autonomous biological simulation engine
with mathematically proven stability, stress resilience, and sovereign
identity management. This white paper establishes the formal system
definition required for monograph integration.

